        {
          "id": "SP_FUNGIACYATHUS_HYDRA_ZIBROWIUS_GILI_1990",
          "name": "Fungiacyathus hydra Zibrowius & Gili, 1990",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Fungiacyathus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(based on Zibrowius and Gill 1990) Corallum small (GCD ~ 9.0 - 12.0 mm), fragile, discoidal, with a slightly concave, convex, or flat base. Calice circular and ~ 5.0 mm in H. Base bear distinct, granular to serrate, costa. C 1 - 2 prominent near calicular margin, becoming less so towards centre of base. C 3 and C 4 unequal and less developed than C 1 and C 2. Intercostal spaces fairly deep and smooth. Corallum white. Septa hexamerally arranged in four cycles according to the formula: S 1> S 2> S 3 - 4 (48 septa). S 1 independent but joining adjacent S 4 by extended synapticular bars. S 2 1 / 4 smaller than S 1, whilst S 3 - 4 are equal in width. S 2 - 4 solidly fused, thus forming distinct delta junctions. Septal faces smooth, with no dentations. Columella absent or may be present as narrow tabular spines",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2260009",
          "authorship": "Zibrowius & Gili",
          "yearPublished": "1990",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "b4e66c36-01e2-54d-98d-27b635baa159cb"
        },
